# Single-page app: every route is served by index.html and resolved by
# react-router in the browser. Without this, refreshing /invoices or opening a
# shared /tickets/GAR-12 link asks Netlify for a file that does not exist and
# gets a 404 — the deep links would work in dev and break in production.
#
# Not forced (no !), so real files still win: /privacy.html and the built
# assets are served as themselves.
# The landing page is a real file at /marketing/index.html (and /ar/). Sent
# there explicitly, so the address without a trailing slash can never fall
# through to the app's rewrite below. Must come first: Netlify stops at the
# first rule that matches.
/marketing     /marketing/     301
/marketing/ar  /marketing/ar/  301

/*  /index.html  200
